    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0802" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v27/pg764"/>

                <head>290. Agreement Between the United States and the United Kingdom<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d290-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                                calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1957-03-27T23:59:59+00:00"
                                notBefore="1957-01-15T00:00:00+00:00"
                        >Undated</date>.</hi></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">AGREEMENT ON LIBYA</p>
                <p>It was agreed that, following the consultations on Libya which had taken place
                    recently in London,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d290-f2"/> a further meeting would be
                    held in Washington in the near future.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d290-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d290-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Conference Files: Lot 62 D 181, CF 868. Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d290-f2" n="2" xml:id="d290-f2-content">
                <p>The U.S.–U.K. discussions on Libya, which took place in London on January 15, are
                    summarized in telegram 3773 from London, January 15, printed in <ref
                        target="frus1955-57v18#pg_465">vol. XVIII, p. 465</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
